# Playtest inbox

Friends Send from the itch playtest build. Those notes become GitHub Issues labeled `playtest` on `Nathan-Elequin/swipe`, through the Cloudflare Worker. That list is the inbox. Do not ask Nathan to paste the notes.

This rule has the same weight as `content-board.mdc` (gold boxes). Do not skip it because the chat is about UI, keys, art, a different card, or process.

Inbox source: Issues created by the playtest build's feedback paths (right-click comment, F2 Feedback, tier list Send). In practice that is label `playtest` on `Nathan-Elequin/swipe`.

This rule fires only in this repo.

Public playtest: https://nathan-elequin.itch.io/spinheritance-playtest (`playtest-ship.mdc`). Local F5 is Godot Play in `C:\Users\Natha\Documents\boss-rush` on branch `playtest/latest`. F5 is **not** itch.

Ledger: `data/playtest-ledger.json`. Board: `playtest/inbox-board.html`. Update both when a ticket changes column.

## Status (three columns)

A ticket has one status. GitHub staying open is not the same as “still broken.”

| Status | What it means | GitHub | Chat section |
|---|---|---|---|
| `todo` | The reported change is **not** on `playtest/latest` in this folder. F5 will still show the old behavior. | Open | **Still broken in F5** |
| `f5` | The change is committed **and** on `playtest/latest` (this checkout). Stop Play, F5, he can try it. Not on itch yet. | Stay open | **Ready in F5** |
| `itch` | The change is on https://nathan-elequin.itch.io/spinheritance-playtest. | Close in that turn | **On itch.io** (once) |

Do not put a ticket in **Ready in F5** because similar code exists, or because a card is in the mill. Only when the *reported* change is in this checkout on `playtest/latest`. Uncommitted WIP does not count. A commit that is only on another branch does not count until it is on `playtest/latest` here.

## Every chat in this repo

Before the requested work, do **all** of:

1. Gold boxes (`content-board.mdc`).
2. Issues with label `playtest` (`gh issue list --label playtest`, open and recently closed).
3. Read `data/playtest-ledger.json`. Reconcile: any open Issue missing from the ledger starts as `todo`. Any ledger `f5` whose SHA is not in this checkout goes back to `todo`. Any ledger `itch` whose GitHub Issue is still open: close GitHub.

Keep tracking **every still-open Issue** in every reply until it is in **On itch.io** or Nathan **verbally describes that ticket as closed**. Then close it on GitHub in that same turn. Do not hide, table, or drop an open Issue because he replied about something else.

Linear bugs (one reading, no new rule, no number change): start the fix in that same turn, commit onto `playtest/latest`, push that branch, set ledger `status` to `f5` with the SHA, and list it under **Ready in F5**. Do not wait for him to say ship. Do **not** butler-push unless he asked (`playtest-ship` wait: uploads are on request). Crashes / cannot-play: same auto-fix.

If a report has two readings that would change the code, Paper Fight. Ask. Do not patch it as a bug.

Balance / “this felt strong”: list it under **Still broken in F5** (Content). Do not change numbers or rules unless he says so in that chat.

Empty **Still broken in F5**: still print the heading, with one line that none are waiting on a local fix.

Empty **Ready in F5**: still print the heading, with one line that nothing new is in this F5 checkout.

Empty **On itch.io**: still print the heading, with one line that none are new to show. That includes the case where every itch close has already been listed in a chat Nathan saw.

In a handoff task (`design/handoff/<task-id>/TASK.md`): only auto-fix if the files are on that task's "Files you may touch" list. Otherwise still list the Issues in the matching column.

## Reply shape in this repo

After the headline, use Next steps (if any), then Notes (if any), then these three sections in this order. They are equal. Neither is Next steps. Neither is Notes.

Topic buckets (use inside **Still broken in F5** and **Ready in F5** when that column has more than a handful; omit empty buckets):

1. **Overall thoughts and core gameplay** — including Challenge, Adventure, the map, and the cabin.
2. **Confusion** — uncertainty, wrong or missing information, inconsistency.
3. **Bugs and visual glitches**
4. **Crashes and cannot-play**
5. **Art and music** — do not draw or replace PNG bytes (`unique-art.mdc`). ART-REQUEST. Do not invent music files unless Nathan asked.
6. **Playtest tooling** — hub, Feedback, tier list, Send, right-click comment.
7. **Content** — item and monster balance, numbered card strength.

### ⬜ Still broken in F5

GitHub Issues labeled `playtest` that are still open **and** whose reported change is not on `playtest/latest` in this folder.

Each item:

- Starts with ⬜
- Issue number, one short line of what they reported, link

Example: `1. ⬜ [#22](url) — Unplayable items (Sledgehammer) should show a grey overlay on the hotbar.`

### 🟩 Ready in F5

Open GitHub Issues whose reported change **is** on `playtest/latest` here. He can Stop Play and F5. Friends on itch will not see it yet. **Do not close GitHub.**

Each item:

- Starts with 🟩
- Issue number, one short line of what to try in F5, link, and the short SHA

Example: `1. 🟩 [#22](url) — Hotbar unplayable overlay. Stop Play, F5. \`abc1234\`.`

Keep listing these every reply until they move to **On itch.io**.

### ✅ On itch.io

Only Issues whose fix you are **confident** is playable on https://nathan-elequin.itch.io/spinheritance-playtest. Local code, F5, or GitHub-only is not enough.

Each item:

- Starts with ✅
- **Bold short phrase** naming the change (not a restatement of the report)
- Then an em dash and one sentence of what you did
- Include the Issue number and link somewhere in that line

Example: `1. ✅ **Unplayable hatch** — Hotbar cards you cannot use get a stripe overlay you can still read through ([#22](url)).`

When that itch bar is met in a chat, close the GitHub Issue in that same turn if it is still open, set ledger `status` to `itch`, and put it here instead of the other two columns. **On itch.io in the reply and closing GitHub are the same action.** If it is in this section, GitHub must already be closed, or you close it before you send the reply.

List an On-itch item **once**. After it has appeared under **On itch.io** (or the old **Closed issues** heading) in a chat message Nathan saw, do not list it again. **Still broken in F5** and **Ready in F5** stay every reply until that ticket qualifies here. Worked example: [#22](https://github.com/Nathan-Elequin/swipe/issues/22) was shown as closed; do not bring it up again.

## Close

Close a GitHub Issue when **either**:

1. Nathan clearly says that ticket is closed / done / finished / live on itch, or
2. The fix is playable on the itch playtest (the bar for **On itch.io**).

Do **not** close GitHub just because F5 works.

Close it yourself in that turn. Do not wait for him to confirm.

How: Shell `gh issue close <n> --repo Nathan-Elequin/swipe`. Do **not** use GitHub MCP `issue_write` (or any MCP that pops a Submit / review card) for this close. Nathan must never open GitHub, click Submit, or approve a close form.

If Auto-review blocks `gh`, retry that same command with `request_smart_mode_approval`. Do not hand him a GitHub click instead.

Do not invent copy to “fix” confusion unless he gave the words. Jam owns `data/player-copy.json`. Unique art still applies.

After a local fix lands on `playtest/latest`, rewrite `playtest/inbox-board.html` from the ledger (three columns) so the board matches chat.

## Do not

- Do not skip this read because the chat is about something else.
- Do not ask Nathan to paste playtest notes.
- Do not stop listing an open Issue until it is live on the itch playtest, or he says to close it.
- Do not mix “fixed in F5” into **Still broken in F5** or into **On itch.io**.
- Do not move an Issue into **On itch.io** because the code exists locally, or because F5 works on this PC.
- Do not list an Issue under **On itch.io** while it is still open on GitHub.
- Do not ask Nathan to close, Submit, or confirm a GitHub Issue. That is your job.
- Do not close a GitHub Issue because he ignored a summary.
- Do not change balance numbers from Content reports unless he says so in that chat.
- Do not treat a gray bug/rule report as a linear bug.
- Do not re-list an On-itch item in a later reply or later chat after it has already appeared under **On itch.io** or **Closed issues** in a message Nathan saw.
